**Pricing Model, Break-Even ****&**** Revenue Projections**

Build New Habits Ltd — 20 Jun 2026 v2 (5 scenarios, 4-year model)

# **1. Confirmed Pricing Structure**

| **Tier** | **Price** | **Notes** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Monthly | £7.99/month | Flat from day one. No introductory rate. |
| Annual | £59.99/year | From launch. Exactly £5/month. No expiry date. |
| Free trial | [LENGTH TBC — 30 days recommended] | Card taken at signup, no payment during trial, reminder before it ends. |
| Beta conversion — annual | £44.99/year | Beta participants only, **December 2026 only**. Locked permanently once taken. |
| Community org — Year 1 | £39.99/year | Via unique code per organisation. Tracked individually. |
| Community org — Year 2+ | £49.99/year | Same model. Modest increase as product proven. |
| Taster code (org members) | 1 month free | Unlocks the Plan for 1 month. Redeemable any time Year 1. |
| Year 2 standard pricing | Deferred | Decided in Year 2, on real data. Subject to rate-never-rises. |

**Changes at 18 Aug 2026, and why — v3.**

**The £4.99 three-month intro is removed.** It removed risk at the point of decision but paid for it with a **60% price rise at month four**, landing exactly when novelty has gone and habit has not formed. It discounted the churn window and then supplied a reason to leave at the end of it. A free trial does the same job at no cost and creates no price rise. The model's own finding stands: **monthly churn, not acquisition, is the real financial risk.**

**Annual is £59.99, not £49.99.** The old £49.99 launch-year window ran to 30 Nov 2026 — **before** the soft launch (first week of December) and two months before public launch (January 2027). It was a price nobody could have paid. Beyond fixing the date: £7.99 × 12 = £95.88, so £49.99 was a **48% discount**, against a more typical 15–20%. £59.99 is still 37% off and is exactly £5/month, which is a line somebody repeats out loud.

**The grandfathering commitment makes every price permanent for the launch cohort.** Nobody's rate ever rises, so a price set now is set forever for the people who join first and stay longest. Underpricing at launch is not a launch decision for them; it is a permanent one. Discounts can always be added later. The rate cannot be raised.

**Beta is £44.99, December 2026 only**, up from £39.99. It keeps the beta rate **under fifty** while standard sits above it — that threshold does real work, and giving it to testers makes their rate feel like the reward it is. The revenue difference across a small beta cohort is trivial; what the standard price signals is not.

**All projections in sections 2–5 below are computed against the OLD prices and are now stale.** They have not been recomputed in this revision. 🟠 Break-even and revenue scenarios need rerunning at £7.99/£59.99 before they are quoted anywhere.

# **2. Startup Costs ****&**** Break-Even**

## **2.1 Startup Costs**

| **Item** | **Cost** | **Notes** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| ICO registration | £40 | Annual. Legally required before collecting user data. |
| Supabase Pro × 3 months | £75 | £25/month. EU region. 3 months pre-launch. |
| Plausible Analytics × 3 months | £27 | £9/month. Privacy-friendly analytics. |
| Public liability insurance | £130 | Annual estimate. |
| Professional indemnity | £200 | Annual. Health-adjacent product. |
| Solicitor (Privacy Policy + T&Cs) | £400 | One-off. Conservative estimate. |
| Domain renewal | £12 | Annual. |
| Zoho Mail | £12 | Annual. £1/month plan. |
| ElevenLabs × 2 months | £44 | Audio content. Starter plan. |
| Sentry | £0 | Free tier sufficient for beta. |
| Stripe | £0 fixed | 2.9% + 30p per transaction. Variable only. |
| Contingency (10%) | £107 |  |
| **TOTAL** | **£1,974** | Rounded to £2,000 seed capital figure |

## **2.2 Break-Even**

| **Route** | **Users needed** | **Net per user** | **Notes** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Monthly @ £7.99 | 267 user-months | £7.76 | e.g. 89 users × 3 months |
| Annual launch @ £49.99 | 41 users | £48.54 | Very achievable within beta conversion alone. |
| Annual standard @ £59.99 | 34 users | £58.25 | Lowest user count to break even. |
| Beta annual @ £39.99 | 52 users | £38.83 |  |
| Community org @ £39.99 | 52 users | £38.83 |  |
| **Mixed (most likely)** | **35–55 users** | Blended | Realistic mix of all tiers. |

*Break-even is a low bar. 34–55 paying users covers the entire £2,000 startup cost. Monthly churn is the real financial risk — not the initial investment.*

# **3. Shared Modelling Assumptions**

| Beta period (Sept–Oct 2026) | Free for all beta participants. No revenue in this period. Data and validation are the return on investment. |
| --- | --- |
| Revenue starts | November 2026 — first conversion offers go out post-beta. |
| Stripe fees | 2.9% + 30p per transaction. Applied throughout. |
| Running costs | £34/month (Supabase £25 + Plausible £9). Scales slightly in Year 3–4. |
| Org outreach | Begins August 2026. Response rate is scenario-dependent. |
| Taster code conversion | Members who redeem a taster code convert to paid at scenario-dependent rates. |
| Annual vs monthly split | 60% annual, 40% monthly across all paid users (except where noted). |
| Year 2 pricing shift | Standard annual rises to £59.99. Community org rises to £49.99. Early adopters locked at their original rate. |
| Learn product (Year 3) | Alongside: Learn launches Year 3. Not modelled in these projections — treated as upside only. |

# **4. Scenario 1 — The Floor**

*Worst realistic case. Not catastrophe — survivability. Assumes minimal org response, very low conversion, high churn. The product exists and grows slowly.*

## **Assumptions**

| Orgs sharing code | 3 agree (6% of 50 contacted). Average 400 members each in comms reach. |
| --- | --- |
| Taster code conversion | 2% of members redeem. 15% of those convert to paid. |
| Beta individual testers | 40 people. 8% convert to paid after beta. |
| General free users (Year 1) | 150 by end of Year 1. |
| Free to paid conversion | 3% |
| Monthly churn | 6% — top of range. |
| Annual:monthly split | 45:55 — fewer commit to annual. |

